---
// SOURCE: zurp-astronomics-site — main site (v2) footer: the footer copy (jokes) on a black band
// AUTHOR: engineer
// DATE: 2026-10-03
// STATUS: active
// REVISED: 2026-10-06 (ticket #49) — every text comes from content/ (site.yml, footer/legalese.md)
//
// The copy began as the v1 footer's, word for word (v1 deleted in ticket #35), and lives in
// content/site.yml (`name`, `affiliation`, `signature`, `org`, `footer`) and content/footer/legalese.md: home line
// (the site's signature) without a product, product line with one.
// The "Low-Tech & DIY" sticker (src/assets/brand/Low_tech_DIY.png, the sticker of the site of
// 8c2fc77) signs the footer of EVERY page of the main site, home included, small (~140 px, the size
// it had there). Ticket #14 had left it out of the home page (its header shows the same poster full
// size); the human found the gap odd, and ticket #16 put it back: do not reintroduce a condition on
// `productName` here, which only picks the footer's copy line. Variants at 140 and 280 px (1x / 2x)
// only: it is never displayed wider. Ticket #35 removed the "v1" link with the v1 archive it led to.
// Ticket #23: the sticker is a link back to the top of the page (`#top`, the id on <body> in
// V2Layout.astro), with nothing visible added — no text, no icon: the human wanted it unannounced,
// the hover (it lights up, as on the old site; it does not move) is the hint. Its accessible name is
// "Back to top" (aria-label), so it is not silent for screen readers. Smooth scroll comes from
// `scroll-behavior` on html, already turned off under prefers-reduced-motion. No JavaScript.
// The look is the old site's footer (src/pages/index.astro of 8c2fc77): raised background, one thin
// rule, the GitHub line in monospace, the signature, the legalese, the sticker.
// `fit="outside"` (ticket #43, Astro 7): the sticker is 1187 × 739 and 140 px gives an 87 px
// height, so Astro 7 asks for its 280 px variant at a rounded height and its image service CROPS to
// that by default. "outside" (sharp's fit: keep the ratio, cover the box) scales instead: the whole
// sticker. `fit` never reaches the HTML.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import sticker from '../../assets/brand/Low_tech_DIY.png';
import { fill, inlineMarkdown, readMarkdown, siteContent, siteView } from '../../lib/content.mjs';

interface Props {
  productName?: string;
}

const { productName } = Astro.props;

const site = siteContent();
const legalese = inlineMarkdown(readMarkdown('footer/legalese.md'));
---

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="z2-container foot-inner">
    <p class="org-link">
      {site.footer.orgLabel} <a href={site.org.url}>{site.org.handle}</a>
    </p>
    {
      productName ? (
        <p>
          <em>{fill(site.footer.productLine, { ...siteView(site), product: productName })}</em>
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          <em>{site.signature}</em>
        </p>
      )
    }
    <p class="legalese" set:html={legalese} />
    <a class="lowtech-link" href="#top" aria-label={site.footer.backToTop}>
      <Image
        src={sticker}
        alt={site.footer.panelAlt}
        title={site.footer.panelTitle}
        width={140}
        widths={[140, 280]}
        fit="outside"
        sizes="140px"
        format="webp"
        quality={72}
        loading="lazy"
        class="lowtech-panel"
      />
    </a>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .foot {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding: 3rem 0;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .foot p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .foot .org-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .foot .legalese {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* The back-to-top link wraps the sticker tightly, so the focus ring draws round it. */
  .lowtech-link {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 1.5rem auto 0;
  }

  /* The old site's sticker (`.easter-egg`), without its tilt and zoom on hover: it lights up only. */
  .lowtech-panel {
    display: block;
    width: 140px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.6;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .lowtech-link:hover,
  .lowtech-link:focus-visible {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .lowtech-link:hover .lowtech-panel,
  .lowtech-link:focus-visible .lowtech-panel {
    opacity: 1;
  }
</style>
